  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to the Multifaceted Crisis of Migrants and Host Communities in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Currently, Egypt, which hosts approximately nine million migrants, faces a multifaceted crisis. The increase in the prices of goods and services experienced in Egypt following the war in the Ukraine and the continued devaluation of the Egyptian pound in 2022-23, pose a significant challenge to the food security and livelihood of migrants and host communities. Furthermore, the war in Sudan that broke out in April 2023 significantly deteriorated the situation. Since April, more than 343,230 people including Egyptian returnees, Sudanese nationals, and third country nationals (TCNs) have fled the war in Sudan to Egypt. This project aims to provide humanitarian assistance, including protection, medical, and mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS), to people in Egypt affected by the crisis in Sudan, including Sudanese new arrivals, Egyptian returnees, and third country nationals, to meet their immediate needs and to create a conducive and sustainable environment, where the migrant population are accepted by the host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
